WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.728
Priya: Make cancellation tests an independent work item. The API contract remains a separate dependency.

2
00:00:07.728 --> 00:00:14.712
Lukas: Does the parser change require that contract? Avoid merging behavior based on guessed semantics.

3
00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:23.040
Raj: Only the integration adapter needs confirmed semantics. Just to confirm, parser review can proceed, right?

4
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:30.984
Anika: Yes, I'll isolate adapter assumptions in fixtures. Maybe the final response changes one test.

5
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:40.416
Hannah: Keep contract tests unapproved until confirmation. Passing local fixtures doesn't certify the real endpoint.

6
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:47.928
Raj: The parser stays up for review today. Its task includes malformed inputs and resource cleanup.

7
00:00:47.928 --> 00:00:54.936
Lukas: The performance benchmark is another separate item. It shouldn't delay functional feedback on parsing.

8
00:00:54.936 --> 00:01:02.544
Priya: Okay, give each action item one owner. Let's park that optional export benchmark for later.

9
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:11.376
Hannah: I'll attach acceptance evidence to each task. That makes partial completion visible without exaggeration.

10
00:01:11.376 --> 00:01:18.240
Anika: Good, the board will show integration waiting. We can finish local work without hiding it.

